 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "seg-01",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "I feel sick today, but an important task waits. After lunch, I check the authentication again. Before the meeting, I review the authorization one more time. The team talks about the access token at the standup. When I use the personal access token, I ask Maria for advice. When we meet, Leo says, \"I don't feel well.\" I reply, \"I have a headache.\" The work is not easy, but I keep going.",
   "tts": "I feel sick today, but an important task waits. After lunch, I check the authentication again. Before the meeting, I review the authorization one more time. The team talks about the access token at the standup. When I use the personal access token, I ask Maria for advice. When we meet, Leo says, \"I don't feel well.\" I reply, \"I have a headache.\" The work is not easy, but I keep going.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-01.mp3",
   "zh": "我今天不太舒服，但一个重要任务在等着我。午饭后，我又检查了一遍身份验证。开会前，我又复习了一遍授权。团队在站会上讨论了访问令牌。使用个人访问令牌时，我向 Maria 请教。见面时，Leo说：\"我感觉不舒服。\"我回答：\"我头痛。\"工作不容易，但我继续前进。",
   "hard": [
    {
     "w": "authentication",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "身份验证，确认用户是谁的过程"
    },
    {
     "w": "authorization",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "授权，确认用户可以做什么的过程"
    },
    {
     "w": "I don't feel well.",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "我感觉不舒服。"
    },
    {
     "w": "I have a headache.",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "我头痛。"
    },
    {
     "w": "access token",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "访问令牌，代替密码授权程序访问服务的字符串"
    },
    {
     "w": "personal access token",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "个人访问令牌，代表个人账号调用 GitHub 的令牌"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "seg-02",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "I visit the pharmacy and ask about the medicine. At the table, Maria says, \"How often should I take this?\" I think, then answer, \"Are there any side effects?\" The team talks about the user account at the standup. When I use the login session, I ask Maria for advice. I compare the repository secret with my notes. Priya and I look for a detail in the workflow permission. I write down what I learned today.",
   "tts": "I visit the pharmacy and ask about the medicine. At the table, Maria says, \"How often should I take this?\" I think, then answer, \"Are there any side effects?\" The team talks about the user account at the standup. When I use the login session, I ask Maria for advice. I compare the repository secret with my notes. Priya and I look for a detail in the workflow permission. I write down what I learned today.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-02.mp3",
   "zh": "我去了药店，询问了这种药。桌边，Maria说：\"这个药多久吃一次？\"我想了想，回答：\"有副作用吗？\"团队在站会上讨论了用户账号。使用登录会话时，我向 Maria 请教。我把仓库机密和我的笔记做了比较。Priya 和我在工作流权限里找一个细节。我记下了今天学到的东西。",
   "hard": [
    {
     "w": "user account",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "用户账号，用来识别和保存个人信息的身份"
    },
    {
     "w": "login session",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "登录会话，用户登录后持续一段时间的访问状态"
    },
    {
     "w": "How often should I take this?",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "这个药多久吃一次？"
    },
    {
     "w": "Are there any side effects?",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "有副作用吗？"
    },
    {
     "w": "repository secret",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "仓库机密，供自动化任务安全使用的敏感值"
    },
    {
     "w": "workflow permission",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "工作流权限，限制自动化可以执行的操作"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "seg-03",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "Before I leave, I review what I did today. After lunch, I check secret scanning again. After I revoke a token, I tell the team. The team talks about the access permission at the standup. Before I sign out, I read the note. When we meet, Leo says, \"I'm allergic to this medicine.\" I reply, \"I need to see a doctor.\" The token is safe, and the secret stays outside the code.",
   "tts": "Before I leave, I review what I did today. After lunch, I check secret scanning again. After I revoke a token, I tell the team. The team talks about the access permission at the standup. Before I sign out, I read the note. When we meet, Leo says, \"I'm allergic to this medicine.\" I reply, \"I need to see a doctor.\" The token is safe, and the secret stays outside the code.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-03.mp3",
   "zh": "离开前，我回顾了今天做的事。午饭后，我又检查了一遍机密扫描。我撤销令牌之后，告诉了团队。团队在站会上讨论了访问权限。在退出登录之前，我先看了说明。见面时，Leo说：\"我对这种药过敏。\"我回答：\"我需要看医生。\"令牌是安全的，机密留在代码之外。",
   "hard": [
    {
     "w": "access permission",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "访问权限，允许用户读取或修改某项资源的规则"
    },
    {
     "w": "sign out",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "退出登录，结束当前登录会话"
    },
    {
     "w": "I'm allergic to this medicine.",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "我对这种药过敏。"
    },
    {
     "w": "I need to see a doctor.",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "我需要看医生。"
    },
    {
     "w": "secret scanning",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "机密扫描，自动发现意外提交的密钥"
    },
    {
     "w": "revoke a token",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "撤销令牌，让已有令牌立即失效"
    }
   ]
  }
